  '## How this file is organized\n' +
  '\n' +
  'The rows are grouped into a tree: capability → feature → subgroup. A capability heading reads\n' +
  '`# CAP-nn · <label>`, a feature heading `## FEAT-nnn · <label>` and a subgroup heading\n' +
  '`### SUB-nnn · <label>`. Each heading is followed by a `Purpose:` line saying why that part of the\n' +
  'product exists. A capability also carries an `Outcome:` line, and a feature a `Status:` line.\n' +
  'A capability may carry five optional lines in any order in its own span. `Kind:` is exactly\n' +
  '`product` or `constraint`; `Deliverables:` lists row IDs, `Needs:` and `Binds:` list capability\n' +
  'IDs, and `Retired:` lists successor capability IDs. A product capability may repeat `Made by:`\n' +
  'and `Read by:` lines for its deliverables, and the tree checker reports gaps in those lines as notes.\n' +
  'A feature under a kinded capability may carry `Artifact: A-nnn · <name> · <class>: <location> · <run>: <writer or reason>` lines after its lifecycle lines and before any subgroup. The six classes are `tracked`, `clone store`, `user-home store`, `other project`, `git ref` and `CI record`; a retired entry keeps its ID with `retired: <reason or successor>` in place of class and run. A feature records a cross-feature read as `Reads: A-nnn · <reader path>[, <reader path>]` after its artifact entries; each reader is a tracked file, and own reads stay implicit. A maker feature declares a reader of its own entry as `Read by: A-nnn · <kind>: <detail>`, where code and prompt name tracked files, person, rule and runtime give reasons, a test file is never a reader, and a currency or presence check is not a reader. Every live entry needs a declared reader or a hold written `Parked: A-nnn · since <YYYY-MM-DD>: <reason>`. A `Made by:` third part names one or more A-IDs directly, or says `built from:` before them.\n' +
